ENTRY            D6497   20260819   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6497001   20260819   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 11         42
TITLE      Investigation of various reaction channels with a 10B
            projectile
AUTHOR     (P.Mishra, V.V.Parkar, S.K.Pandit, S.Kaur, A.Chavan,
            K.Mahata, A.Shrivastava, K.Ramachandran, V.Kumar,
            S.Dhuri, M.Prasanna, S.Rathi)
INSTITUTE  (3INDTRM)
           (3INDIND) Rani Channamma University, Belagavi
           (3INDIND) Homi Bhabha National Institute,
            Anushaktinagar, Mumbai
           (3INDIND) Vivekanand Education Society's College of
            Arts, Science and Commerce, Mumbai
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,111,054608,2025)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.111.054608
           (J,NP/A,1065,123264,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysa.2025.123264
            Conf. proc. (ICNPA-2024). Same 209Bi data in figures
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDTAT) BARC-TIFR Pelletron LINAC Facility
SAMPLE     Self-supporting foils of 159Tb, 197Au, and 209Bi of
            thicknesses ~1 mg/cm2.
DETECTOR   (TELES,SISD,SISD) Five Si-strip detector of
            thicknesses of deltaE strip detectors were 50 um for
            first, second and third and 30 um for fourth and
            fifth while the E strip detectors were of thicknesses
            1.5 mm for first, second and third, 1 mm for fourth
            and 150 um for fifth. The active area of the Si-strip
            detectors was 50 X 50 mm2 and the width of each strip
            was 3.1 mm.
           (TELES,SIBAR) Three SSB detector telescopes, the
            thicknesses of the deltaE detectors were 50 um for
            first and 27 um for second and third while all three
            E detectors were of 1 mm thickness. The angular range
            covered with the detector setup was from 30 to
            140 degree.
           (SIBAR) Two SSB detectors with thicknesses ~300 um
            were kept at +/-20 degree for absolute normalization
            and beam monitoring.
METHOD     (EDE)
CORRECTION Beam energy was corrected for the energy loss at half
            the target thickness.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on the source of uncertainty
HISTORY    (20260218R) Data received from P.Mishra (2026-02-18)
           (20260819C) A.Gandhi
ENDBIB              42
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           45
